{"id": "WQ-SEED-04", "surface": "will_question", "description": "the ask is the speaker's own words", "input": {"title": "Pilot proposal", "transcript": "Thank you all for coming. The pilot saved our support team hours every week. My ask is simple: approve the pilot today."}, "rubric": {"expect_contains": {"ask": "approve the pilot"}, "semantic_intent": "ask is a short phrase copied from the transcript asking to approve the pilot; audience is empty or a phrase the transcript says."}}
// The light touch (founder 2026-10-20, N86): a row with a key and a question runs ``vary``; the output is {"question", "varied"}. A variation that fails read_varied falls back to the signed words, so "question" is always a question Will may ask.
{"id": "WQ-VARY-01", "surface": "will_question", "description": "the audience question, said with a light touch, still asks who the talk is for", "input": {"key": "audience", "question": "Quick one: who's this talk really for? 🎯"}, "rubric": {"no_digits": true, "max_chars": 200, "must_mention_substrings": ["?"], "semantic_intent": "a short friendly question asking who the speaker's talk is really for; the same meaning as 'Quick one: who's this talk really for?', no advice, no new facts."}}
{"id": "WQ-VARY-02", "surface": "will_question", "description": "the goal question keeps its two halves: do, or feel", "input": {"key": "goal", "question": "When you finish, what do you want them to do? Or feel? 🤔"}, "rubric": {"no_digits": true, "max_chars": 200, "must_mention_substrings": ["?"], "semantic_intent": "asks what the speaker wants the audience to do or feel when the talk ends; the same meaning as 'When you finish, what do you want them to do? Or feel?'"}}
{"id": "WQ-VARY-03", "surface": "will_question", "description": "the speaker's own words stay in place, once", "input": {"key": "audience_check", "question": "Sounds like this one's for {heard}. Right? 🎯"}, "rubric": {"no_digits": true, "max_chars": 200, "must_mention_substrings": ["{heard}", "?"], "semantic_intent": "a check that the talk is for {heard}, asking the speaker to confirm; the placeholder {heard} appears exactly once."}}
{"id": "WQ-VARY-04", "surface": "will_question", "description": "the practised line stays in place, once", "input": {"key": "not_used", "question": "Last time we practised “{words}”. It didn't make it into this Take. On purpose? 😏"}, "rubric": {"no_digits": true, "max_chars": 200, "must_mention_substrings": ["{words}", "?"], "semantic_intent": "says the line {words} practised last time did not come back in this Take and asks whether that was on purpose; {words} appears exactly once."}}
{"id": "WQ-VARY-05", "surface": "will_question", "description": "the breather question still offers both: a breather, or something missing", "input": {"key": "pause", "question": "You've put real work into this one 💪 Need a breather, or does something feel missing?"}, "rubric": {"no_digits": true, "max_chars": 200, "must_mention_substrings": ["?"], "semantic_intent": "acknowledges the speaker's effort and asks whether they need a breather or something feels missing; the same meaning as the signed question."}}
